  "question": {
    "text": "A perfect gas at $27^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ is heated at constant pressure so as to double its volume. The final temperature of the gas will be, close to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "y3yaW",
      "text": "\n$327^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "UxBHc",
      "text": "\n$200^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "LnlmT",
      "text": "\n$54^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "SRoRR",
      "text": "\n$300^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given, $V_1=V$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& V_2=2 V \\\\\n& T_1=27^{\\circ}+273=300 \\mathrm{~K} \\\\\n& T_2=?\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nFrom charle's law\n$$\n\\frac{V_1}{T_1}=\\frac{V_2}{T_2}(\\because \\text { Pressure is constant })\n$$\nor, $\\frac{V}{300}=\\frac{2 V}{T_2}$\n\n$$\n\\therefore \\quad T_2=600 \\mathrm{~K}=600-273=327^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
